<!-- ═══ EU 2026 REGULATIONS ═══ -->
<section style="padding: 5.5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #111; background: #040404;">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="label">EU Regulatory Landscape 2026</p>
    <h2 class="h2" style="margin-bottom: 1rem; max-width: 640px;">
      What EU brands sourcing apparel need to know before placing orders in 2026
    </h2>
    <p class="body-text" style="max-width: 680px; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      Three significant EU regulations are shaping what apparel manufacturers need to provide, and what brands need to document, from 2026 onwards. Most manufacturers are not ready. SDF is.
    </p>
    <div class="grid-1px" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));">
      <div class="cell" style="padding: 2.5rem;">
        <p class="label">EU Digital Product Passport</p>
        <h3 style="font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">Ecodesign for Sustainable Products Regulation (ESPR)</h3>
        <p class="body-text" style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          Phasing in from 2026, the DPP requires a digital record per product covering: materials and their origin, production location, certification status, carbon footprint data, repairability score, and end-of-life guidance.
        </p>
        <p class="body-text">
          SDF provides full material traceability documentation with every order — fabric origin, yarn source, dye certifications, and all 13 active compliance certificates. This covers the majority of DPP data requirements.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell" style="padding: 2.5rem;">
        <p class="label">EU CSDDD</p>
        <h3 style="font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">Corporate Sustainability Due Diligence Directive</h3>
        <p class="body-text" style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          Requires EU companies above certain thresholds to conduct and document human rights and environmental due diligence across their supply chain — including their apparel manufacturers. Non-compliance means fines of up to 5% of global net turnover.
        </p>
        <p class="body-text">
          SDF holds BSCI, SEDEX SMETA, SA8000, WRAP, and ISO 14001 — the core certifications that satisfy CSDDD supplier requirements. Audit reports from our most recent assessments are available to buyers under NDA.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell" style="padding: 2.5rem;">
        <p class="label">EU Green Claims Directive</p>
        <h3 style="font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">Substantiating Sustainability Claims</h3>
        <p class="body-text" style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          From 2026, EU brands can only make environmental claims on their products if those claims are backed by recognised third-party certification. "Sustainable", "eco-friendly", and "natural" without a certificate are illegal under this directive.
        </p>
        <p class="body-text">
          GOTS, GRS, OEKO-TEX, and OCS — all held by SDF — are specifically recognised under the Green Claims Directive as acceptable evidence. Every order produced under these certifications comes with the transaction certificate required for compliant claim use.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="note" style="margin-top: 1.5rem; max-width: 600px;">
      Use our <a href="/tools/eu-readiness-checker" class="inline">EU Readiness Checker</a> to assess your current compliance position before placing an order.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

