    <h2 class="h2" style="margin-bottom: 3rem; max-width: 500px;">Apparel manufacturing — what buyers ask most</h2>
    <div style="max-width: 800px;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 style="font-size: 0.92rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">What is the difference between OEM, ODM, and CMT?</h3>
        <p class="body-text">OEM: you provide the spec, we source and produce. ODM/private label: we develop the design from your brief, you approve, we produce. CMT: you supply the fabric, we cut, sew, and finish. SDF offers all three from 300 pieces. The right model depends on how developed your product is and how much control you want over raw materials.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 style="font-size: 0.92rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">What certifications do I need for EU market access in 2026?</h3>
        <p class="body-text">At minimum: GOTS or OEKO-TEX for product safety claims, BSCI or SEDEX for social compliance, and ISO 14001 for environmental management. From 2026, EU CSDDD also requires supply chain due diligence documentation from your manufacturer. SDF provides all of this. We also provide material traceability documentation for EU Digital Product Passport requirements.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 style="font-size: 0.92rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">What does AQL 2.5 actually mean?</h3>
        <p class="body-text">It means that if more than 2.5% of the inspected batch has defects, the entire batch is rejected and reworked. In practice: fewer than 1 in 40 garments will have a defect leaving our facility. AQL 4.0 — used by many budget factories — accepts twice the defect rate. Our AQL team is in-house and present throughout production, not just at the end.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 style="font-size: 0.92rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">What is the MOQ?</h3>
        <p class="body-text">300 pieces per style. You can split that across sizes and up to 2 colourways within the same style. This minimum is fixed — we cannot go below it for certified production that covers material sourcing, sampling, and full QC. For orders above 1,000 pieces, pricing improves meaningfully per unit.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 style="font-size: 0.92rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">How does FOB pricing work?</h3>
        <p class="body-text">FOB Chittagong covers everything from fabric sourcing through to loading at port — including AQL inspection, labelling, poly bag packaging, and export documentation. Your freight forwarder handles ocean or air freight from that point. We do not add hidden charges at invoice. The price you are quoted is the price you pay to us.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 style="font-size: 0.92rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">What are the payment terms?</h3>
        <p class="body-text">30% deposit to confirm the order and start production. 70% balance before shipment. Accepted via T/T, L/C, or bank transfer. We do not require full prepayment. For clients with an established order history, extended terms are discussed on a case-by-case basis.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
